window.ZELIX_DOCS_INDEX = [{"title": "bspwm", "url": "docs-desktop-bspwm.html#desktop-bspwm", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides bspwm \n\t\t\t\t\t bspwm bspwm is an X11 tiling window manager controlled through  bspc . Its startup script is usually  ~/.config/bspwm/bspwmrc . Keyboard shortcuts are handled separately by  sxhkd , commonly configured in  ~/.config/sxhkd/sxhkdrc . A desktop with no working shortcuts may simply have an inactive sxhkd process. Useful checks:   bspc query -M  lists monitors. Check  pgrep -a sxhkd  when shortcuts fail. After editing the startup script,  bspc wm -r  restarts bspwm; save work first and keep a terminal open. pgrep -a sxhkd bspc query -M bspwm documentation ZelixOS setup ZelixOS adds border, gap and feh wallpaper commands to  ~/.config/bspwm/bspwmrc . Back up the script before editing, and keep it executable. The window manager and sxhkd are separate processes; inspect  ~/.config/sxhkd/sxhkdrc  for your actual bindings. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri bspwm \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t bspwm bspwm,  bspc  ile denetlenen bir X11 pencere yöneticisidir. Başlangıç betiği genellikle  ~/.config/bspwm/bspwmrc  konumundadır. Klavye kısayolları ayrı çalışan  sxhkd  tarafından yönetilir; yapılandırması çoğunlukla  ~/.config/sxhkd/sxhkdrc  konumundadır. Kısayollar çalışmıyorsa sxhkd etkin olmayabilir. Yararlı kontroller:   bspc query -M  ekranları listeler. Kısayollar için  pgrep -a sxhkd  ile süreci kontrol edin. Başlangıç betiğini düzenledikten sonra  bspc wm -r  bspwm’yi yeniden başlatır; önce çalışmanızı kaydedip bir terminali açık tutun. pgrep -a sxhkd bspc query -M bspwm belgeleri ZelixOS kurulumu ZelixOS  ~/.config/bspwm/bspwmrc  içine kenarlık, boşluk ve feh duvar kâğıdı komutları ekler. Betiği düzenlemeden önce yedekleyin ve çalıştırılabilir durumda tutun. Pencere yöneticisi ve sxhkd ayrı süreçlerdir; kısayolları  ~/.config/sxhkd/sxhkdrc  dosyasından inceleyin. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "GNOME", "url": "docs-desktop-gnome.html#desktop-gnome", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides GNOME \n\t\t\t\t\t GNOME GNOME centers work around Activities, the app grid, search, and workspaces. Use Settings for Displays, Sound, Keyboard, Power, and Privacy. On a laptop, check Power and touchpad settings first. GNOME extensions can alter the shell; if a problem begins after enabling one, turn that extension off and test again. Useful checks:  Open Settings with  gnome-control-center  when the app menu works poorly. Check the selected output device in Sound and the monitor layout in Displays. For a login loop, choose the GNOME session on the greeter, then collect the user journal from a text console. gnome-control-center GNOME help ZelixOS setup Open Activities to search for applications and move between workspaces. In Settings → Keyboard you can review and change shortcuts. Disable recently added extensions when diagnosing a shell problem. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Everyday use Activities and workspaces Open Activities to search for applications and view open windows. Use the workspace overview to organize tasks and move between workspaces. Review the installed shortcuts in Settings → Keyboard rather than assuming a particular key binding. Everyday settings In Settings, configure displays, keyboard input, sound devices and power behavior. On a laptop, review touchpad and suspend settings. If an external display is missing, check its cable and selected input before changing the layout. Extensions and session issues Extensions can change shell behavior. If a problem starts after installing or updating one, disable that extension and test again. For login loops, select GNOME at the greeter, check free space and follow  troubleshooting  to collect the user journal.", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri GNOME \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t GNOME GNOME, Etkinlikler görünümü, uygulama ızgarası, arama ve çalışma alanları etrafında kullanılır. Ekran, Ses, Klavye, Güç ve Gizlilik için Ayarlar’ı açın. Dizüstünde önce güç ve dokunmatik yüzey ayarlarına bakın. GNOME eklentileri kabuğu değiştirebilir; bir sorun eklenti etkinleştirildikten sonra başladıysa eklentiyi kapatıp yeniden deneyin. Yararlı kontroller:  Uygulama menüsü sorunluysa Ayarlar’ı  gnome-control-center  ile açın. Ses bölümünde çıkış aygıtını, Ekranlar’da monitör düzenini kontrol edin. Giriş döngüsü yaşanıyorsa giriş ekranında GNOME oturumunu seçin ve metin konsolundan kullanıcı günlüğünü toplayın. gnome-control-center GNOME yardımı ZelixOS kurulumu Uygulamaları aramak ve çalışma alanları arasında geçmek için Etkinlikler’i açın. Ayarlar → Klavye bölümünden kısayolları inceleyip değiştirebilirsiniz. Kabuk sorunu yaşarsanız son eklediğiniz uzantıları devre dışı bırakın. \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Günlük kullanım Etkinlikler ve çalışma alanları Uygulamaları aramak ve açık pencereleri görmek için Etkinlikler’i açın. İşleri düzenlemek ve çalışma alanları arasında geçmek için genel görünümü kullanın. Belirli bir kısayımı varsaymak yerine Ayarlar → Klavye bölümündeki kurulu kısayolları inceleyin. Günlük ayarlar Ayarlar üzerinden ekranları, klavye girişini, ses aygıtlarını ve güç davranışını yapılandırın. Dizüstünde dokunmatik yüzey ve askıya alma ayarlarını gözden geçirin. Harici ekran görünmüyorsa düzeni değiştirmeden önce kabloyu ve monitörün giriş seçimini kontrol edin. Eklentiler ve oturum sorunları Eklentiler kabuğun davranışını değiştirebilir. Sorun bir eklentiyi kurduktan veya güncelledikten sonra başladıysa eklentiyi kapatıp yeniden deneyin. Giriş döngüsünde giriş ekranından GNOME’u seçin, boş alanı kontrol edin ve kullanıcı günlüğünü toplamak için  sorun giderme  rehberini izleyin."}, {"title": "Hyprland", "url": "docs-desktop-hyprland.html#desktop-hyprland", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides Hyprland \n\t\t\t\t\t Hyprland Hyprland is a Wayland compositor with dynamic tiling. Review  ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf  or  ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua  for your actual key bindings, monitor rules, startup apps, and input layout. Shortcuts shown in another distribution's guide may not match ZelixOS. Back up this file before editing it. Useful checks:   hyprctl monitors  lists detected displays;  hyprctl devices  lists input devices;  hyprctl reload  rereads the configuration after a change. For a black screen after editing, restore the last working config from a text console. Screen sharing and file picker issues can also involve the desktop portal, so record the affected app and session type. hyprctl monitors hyprctl reload Hyprland documentation ZelixOS setup ZelixOS installs Waybar, Wofi and swaybg. Waybar starts with the session; Super + Space opens Wofi. If the bar or launcher is missing, inspect the ZelixOS fragment and check whether the commands exist with  command -v waybar wofi swaybg . The fragment may be  ~/.config/hypr/zelix.conf  or  ~/.config/hypr/zelix.lua ; preserve its include in the main config. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri Hyprland \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Hyprland Hyprland, dinamik döşemeli bir Wayland bileştiricisidir. Gerçek kısayollar, ekran kuralları, başlangıç uygulamaları ve klavye düzeni için  ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf  veya  ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua  dosyasını inceleyin. Başka bir dağıtımın kısayolları ZelixOS ile aynı olmayabilir. Düzenlemeden önce dosyanın yedeğini alın. Yararlı kontroller:   hyprctl monitors  algılanan ekranları,  hyprctl devices  giriş aygıtlarını listeler;  hyprctl reload  değişikliklerden sonra yapılandırmayı yeniden okur. Düzenleme sonrası siyah ekran olursa metin konsolundan çalışan son yapılandırmayı geri yükleyin. Ekran paylaşımı ve dosya seçici sorunlarında masaüstü portalı da etkili olabilir; uygulama adını ve oturum türünü kaydedin. hyprctl monitors hyprctl reload Hyprland belgeleri ZelixOS kurulumu ZelixOS Waybar, Wofi ve swaybg kurar. Waybar oturumla başlar; Super + Space Wofi’yi açar. Çubuk veya başlatıcı görünmüyorsa ZelixOS yapılandırma parçasını inceleyin ve  command -v waybar wofi swaybg  ile komutları kontrol edin. Parça  ~/.config/hypr/zelix.conf  veya  ~/.config/hypr/zelix.lua  olabilir; ana yapılandırmadaki bağlantısını koruyun. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "i3", "url": "docs-desktop-i3.html#desktop-i3", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides i3 \n\t\t\t\t\t i3 i3 is a tiling window manager for X11. Its configuration is commonly stored at  ~/.config/i3/config . Read that file for the chosen Mod key, terminal, launcher, workspace bindings, and status bar. i3's first-run configuration may ask you to choose a Mod key. Useful checks:   i3-msg reload  rereads the config;  i3-msg -t get_outputs  lists outputs. A config syntax or missing launcher command can make shortcuts appear broken. Use  i3 -C  to validate the configuration before restarting the session. i3 -C i3-msg reload i3 user guide ZelixOS setup ZelixOS includes  ~/.config/i3/zelix.conf  from the main config for borders, gaps and wallpaper via feh. Back up both files before editing; keep the include if you want these defaults. Review the actual bindings in your config instead of assuming a particular Mod key. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri i3 \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t i3 i3, X11 için döşemeli pencere yöneticisidir. Yapılandırma genellikle  ~/.config/i3/config  konumundadır. Mod tuşu, terminal, başlatıcı, çalışma alanı kısayolları ve durum çubuğu için bu dosyayı okuyun. İlk açılışta Mod tuşunu seçmeniz istenebilir. Yararlı kontroller:   i3-msg reload  yapılandırmayı yeniden okur;  i3-msg -t get_outputs  ekranları listeler. Yapılandırma hatası veya eksik başlatıcı komutu kısayolları bozuk gösterebilir. Oturumu yeniden başlatmadan önce  i3 -C  ile dosyayı doğrulayın. i3 -C i3-msg reload i3 kullanım kılavuzu ZelixOS kurulumu ZelixOS kenarlık, boşluk ve feh ile duvar kâğıdı için  ~/.config/i3/zelix.conf  dosyasını ana yapılandırmaya dahil eder. Düzenlemeden önce iki dosyayı da yedekleyin; bu varsayılanları korumak için include satırını bırakın. Mod tuşunu ve kısayolları kendi yapılandırmanızdan kontrol edin. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "KDE Plasma", "url": "docs-desktop-plasma.html#desktop-plasma", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides KDE Plasma \n\t\t\t\t\t KDE Plasma The styled Plasma desktop is the main ZelixOS experience. Use System Settings for display arrangement and scaling, keyboard layouts, audio, power, and workspace behavior. Right-click the desktop or panel to adjust widgets. KRunner opens apps and searches commands; the launcher shortcut may depend on the installed configuration. Useful checks:  Open System Settings from the app menu or with  systemsettings . If panels disappear while apps still work, first log out and back in. If only one display is missing, check System Settings → Display and Monitor and inspect its enabled state and refresh rate. Record whether the session is Wayland or X11 before reporting rendering problems. systemsettings KDE documentation ZelixOS setup Start with the application launcher and System Settings. The panel and its widgets can be customized from their context menus. If more than one desktop is installed, choose Plasma on the login screen before signing in. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Everyday use Getting around Open the application launcher to find installed programs, and use the panel to switch between windows. Use the desktop and panel context menus to adjust widgets; record your preferred layout before making large changes. Displays, input and sound Open System Settings to arrange monitors, set scaling and select keyboard layouts. Check the selected input and output in Sound when a microphone or speakers do not work. Apply display changes only after checking that each screen remains usable. Session and troubleshooting Choose Plasma at the login screen if multiple sessions are installed. To identify the current session type, run  echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE  in a terminal. If login returns to the greeter, check free space and collect the user journal as described in  troubleshooting .", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri KDE Plasma \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t KDE Plasma ZelixOS’un öne çıkan görünümlü masaüstü Plasma’dır. Ekran düzeni ve ölçekleme, klavye, ses, güç ve çalışma alanı davranışı için Sistem Ayarları’nı kullanın. Araç takımlarını düzenlemek için masaüstüne veya panele sağ tıklayın. KRunner uygulama açar ve komut arar; kısayolu kurulu yapılandırmaya bağlı olabilir. Yararlı kontroller:  Sistem Ayarları’nı uygulama menüsünden veya  systemsettings  ile açın. Uygulamalar çalışırken yalnızca panel kaybolursa önce oturumu kapatıp yeniden açın. Tek bir ekran görünmüyorsa Sistem Ayarları → Ekran ve Monitör bölümünde etkinlik durumunu ve yenileme hızını kontrol edin. Görüntü hatasını bildirirken oturumun Wayland mı X11 mi olduğunu kaydedin. systemsettings KDE belgeleri ZelixOS kurulumu Uygulama başlatıcısı ve Sistem Ayarları ile başlayın. Paneli ve araç takımlarını sağ tık menülerinden düzenleyebilirsiniz. Birden fazla masaüstü kuruluysa giriş ekranında Plasma oturumunu seçin. \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Günlük kullanım Masaüstünde gezinme Kurulu programları uygulama başlatıcısından bulun; pencereler arasında geçmek için paneli kullanın. Araç takımlarını masaüstünün ve panelin sağ tık menülerinden düzenleyin; büyük değişikliklerden önce tercih ettiğiniz düzeni not edin. Ekran, giriş ve ses Monitörleri düzenlemek, ölçeklemeyi ve klavye düzenlerini seçmek için Sistem Ayarları’nı açın. Mikrofon veya hoparlör çalışmıyorsa Ses bölümündeki giriş ve çıkışı kontrol edin. Ekran değişikliklerini uygularken her ekranın kullanılabilir kaldığını doğrulayın. Oturum ve sorun giderme Birden fazla oturum kuruluysa giriş ekranında Plasma’yı seçin. Oturum türünü görmek için terminalde  echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE  çalıştırın. Giriş ekranına geri dönüyorsanız boş alanı kontrol edin ve  sorun giderme  rehberindeki kullanıcı günlüğünü toplayın."}, {"title": "Sway", "url": "docs-desktop-sway.html#desktop-sway", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides Sway \n\t\t\t\t\t Sway Sway is an i3-style Wayland compositor. Check  ~/.config/sway/config  for actual shortcuts and output settings. Its example configuration commonly uses the Mod key with Enter for a terminal and Mod+Shift+C to reload, but verify the installed config first. Useful checks:   swaymsg -t get_outputs  identifies displays and modes;  swaymsg -t get_inputs  identifies keyboards and pointing devices;  swaymsg reload  applies configuration changes. If a monitor stays dark, inspect its output name before adding an output rule. swaymsg -t get_outputs swaymsg reload Sway documentation ZelixOS setup ZelixOS adds  ~/.config/sway/zelix.conf  for borders, gaps and wallpaper, included from the main config. Back up both files before editing. Use  sway -C  to check configuration syntax before reloading; inspect any reported line and keep a terminal open. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri Sway \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Sway Sway, i3 tarzında bir Wayland bileştiricisidir. Gerçek kısayollar ve ekran ayarları için  ~/.config/sway/config  dosyasını kontrol edin. Örnek yapılandırmada terminal için Mod+Enter, yeniden yükleme için Mod+Shift+C yaygındır; önce kurulu dosyayı doğrulayın. Yararlı kontroller:   swaymsg -t get_outputs  ekranları ve modları,  swaymsg -t get_inputs  klavye ve işaretleme aygıtlarını listeler;  swaymsg reload  yapılandırmayı uygular. Ekran karanlık kalırsa çıkış kuralı eklemeden önce çıkış adını belirleyin. swaymsg -t get_outputs swaymsg reload Sway belgeleri ZelixOS kurulumu ZelixOS kenarlık, boşluk ve duvar kâğıdı için ana dosyadan dahil edilen  ~/.config/sway/zelix.conf  dosyasını ekler. Düzenlemeden önce iki dosyayı da yedekleyin. Yeniden yüklemeden önce  sway -C  ile sözdizimini kontrol edin; bildirilen satırı inceleyin ve terminali açık tutun. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Xfce", "url": "docs-desktop-xfce.html#desktop-xfce", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Desktop guides Xfce \n\t\t\t\t\t Xfce Xfce uses a classic panel, application menu, and configurable desktop. Its components are modular, so a missing panel does not always mean the whole session has failed. Use Settings Manager for displays, keyboard, appearance, and window behavior; use the panel's context menu to adjust launchers. Useful checks:  Open Settings Manager with  xfce4-settings-manager . If the panel alone has disappeared, run  xfce4-panel --restart  from a terminal in the Xfce session. If the desktop is blank, check whether you selected the Xfce session at login before changing autostart entries. xfce4-settings-manager xfce4-panel --restart Xfce documentation ZelixOS setup Use Settings Manager → Session and Startup to review startup applications, and Panel preferences to arrange launchers. The installer supplies the Materia GTK theme, Adwaita icons and a dedicated wallpaper. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Everyday use Panel and applications Use the application menu to start programs and the panel to switch windows. Right-click the panel to open its preferences and arrange items or launchers. Record your layout before making extensive changes. Settings and startup Open Settings Manager for displays, keyboard, appearance and window behavior. In Session and Startup, review applications that start with your session; disable an entry only after identifying what it does. See  visual themes  for appearance guidance. Panel or desktop problems If only the panel is missing, open a terminal in the Xfce session and run  xfce4-panel --restart . If the entire session fails, check the selected session and free space, then follow  troubleshooting . Back up configuration before changing or removing it.", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Masaüstü rehberleri Xfce \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Xfce Xfce klasik panel, uygulama menüsü ve yapılandırılabilir masaüstü sunar. Bileşenleri ayrıdır; panelin kaybolması her zaman tüm oturumun çöktüğü anlamına gelmez. Ekran, klavye, görünüm ve pencere davranışı için Ayar Yöneticisi’ni; başlatıcılar için panelin sağ tık menüsünü kullanın. Yararlı kontroller:  Ayar Yöneticisi’ni  xfce4-settings-manager  ile açın. Yalnız panel kaybolduysa Xfce oturumundaki terminalden  xfce4-panel --restart  çalıştırın. Masaüstü boşsa başlangıç girdilerini değiştirmeden önce girişte Xfce oturumunu seçtiğinizi doğrulayın. xfce4-settings-manager xfce4-panel --restart Xfce belgeleri ZelixOS kurulumu Başlangıç uygulamaları için Ayar Yöneticisi → Oturum ve Başlangıç bölümünü, başlatıcıları düzenlemek için Panel tercihlerini kullanın. Kurucu Materia GTK temasını, Adwaita simgelerini ve özel duvar kâğıdını sağlar. \n\t\t\t\t \n                     Günlük kullanım Panel ve uygulamalar Programları uygulama menüsünden açın ve pencereler arasında panelden geçin. Panele sağ tıklayarak tercihleri açın; öğeleri veya başlatıcıları düzenleyin. Kapsamlı değişikliklerden önce düzeninizi not edin. Ayarlar ve başlangıç Ekran, klavye, görünüm ve pencere davranışı için Ayar Yöneticisi’ni açın. Oturum ve Başlangıç bölümünde oturumla açılan uygulamaları inceleyin; bir girdiyi yalnızca ne yaptığını öğrendikten sonra kapatın. Görünüm için  görsel temalar  rehberine bakın. Panel veya masaüstü sorunları Yalnızca panel kaybolduysa Xfce oturumunda bir terminal açıp  xfce4-panel --restart  çalıştırın. Oturumun tamamı açılmıyorsa seçilen oturumu ve boş alanı kontrol edip  sorun giderme  rehberini izleyin. Yapılandırmayı değiştirmeden veya silmeden önce yedekleyin."}, {"title": "Desktop environments", "url": "docs-desktops.html#desktops", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Desktop environments \n\t\t\t\t\t The default ZelixOS experience shown with KDE Plasma. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t KDE Plasma GNOME Xfce Hyprland Sway i3 bspwm \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The installer presents the available desktops and window managers. Choose one or more during installation; the exact list and default shortcuts can change with the ISO. KDE Plasma and GNOME are full desktop environments. Xfce is a lighter traditional desktop. Hyprland, Sway, i3, and bspwm are window managers: expect to configure shortcuts, a launcher, notifications, and sometimes screen sharing yourself. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t First identify your session Run these commands inside the installed desktop, not from the live USB. A blank value does not necessarily mean the session is broken. Read your session name on the login screen too. printf '%s\\n' \"$XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\" \"$XDG_SESSION_TYPE\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Login managers and session selection SDDM, GDM, LightDM, and Ly can offer different session selectors. Choose the desktop you installed before entering your password. If an unfamiliar desktop opens, sign out and select the intended session. The selected login manager also determines whether the ZelixOS SDDM theme appears. Do not enable two login managers at once. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Desktop environments \n\t\t\t\t\t The default ZelixOS experience shown with KDE Plasma. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t KDE Plasma GNOME Xfce Hyprland Sway i3 bspwm \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Yükleyici, kullanılabilir masaüstü ortamlarını ve pencere yöneticilerini gösterir. Kurulum sırasında bir veya daha fazla ortam seçin; kesin liste ve varsayılan kısayollar ISO’ya göre değişebilir. KDE Plasma ve GNOME tam masaüstü ortamlarıdır. Xfce daha hafif, geleneksel bir masaüstüdür. Hyprland, Sway, i3 ve bspwm pencere yöneticileridir: kısayolları, uygulama başlatıcıyı, bildirimleri ve kimi zaman ekran paylaşımını kendiniz yapılandırmanız gerekebilir. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Önce oturumunuzu belirleyin Bu komutları canlı USB yerine kurulu masaüstünde çalıştırın. Boş değer, oturumun mutlaka bozuk olduğu anlamına gelmez. Giriş ekranındaki oturum adını da kontrol edin. printf '%s\\n' \"$XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\" \"$XDG_SESSION_TYPE\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Giriş yöneticileri ve oturum seçimi SDDM, GDM, LightDM ve Ly farklı oturum seçicileri sunabilir. Parolayı girmeden kurduğunuz masaüstünü seçin. Yanlış masaüstü açılırsa çıkış yapıp doğru oturumu seçin. Hangi giriş yöneticisinin seçildiği ZelixOS SDDM temasının görünüp görünmeyeceğini de belirler. Aynı anda iki giriş yöneticisini etkinleştirmeyin. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Why ZelixOS?", "url": "docs-introduction.html#introduction", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Getting started Why ZelixOS? \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution designed to provide a streamlined desktop while preserving the flexibility of its underlying system. Install once and receive ongoing software and kernel updates through the rolling release model. \n\t\t\t\t\t The system favors a clean starting point over a large collection of preinstalled applications. Its custom tools help with setup and maintenance, while desktop and window manager choices let you shape the system around your workflow. ZelixOS includes a graphical installer, a welcome utility, an updater, and command-line helpers to make common tasks easier to discover. \n\t\t\t\t\t Rolling release, familiar tools Software is delivered continuously from the Arch ecosystem. For applications shown in Zelix Hello, use its Software page first. Pacman manages official repository packages. During installation, you choose whether to install an AUR helper. Check that choice on your own system before following helper commands; keep regular backups of important files. \n\t\t\t\t\t A clean KDE Plasma workspace with ZelixOS styling. \n\t\t\t\t\t Official website For current downloads, release information, and community links, visit  zelixos.com . \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Getting started Why ZelixOS? \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution designed to provide a streamlined desktop while preserving the flexibility of its underlying system. Install once and receive ongoing software and kernel updates through the rolling release model. \n\t\t\t\t\t The system favors a clean starting point over a large collection of preinstalled applications. Its custom tools help with setup and maintenance, while desktop and window manager choices let you shape the system around your workflow. ZelixOS includes a graphical installer, a welcome utility, an updater, and command-line helpers to make common tasks easier to discover. \n\t\t\t\t\t Rolling release, familiar tools Software is delivered continuously from the Arch ecosystem. For applications shown in Zelix Hello, use its Software page first. Pacman manages official repository packages. During installation, you choose whether to install an AUR helper. Check that choice on your own system before following helper commands; keep regular backups of important files. \n\t\t\t\t\t A clean KDE Plasma workspace with ZelixOS styling. \n\t\t\t\t\t Official website For current downloads, release information, and community links, visit  zelixos.com . \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "System requirements", "url": "docs-requirements.html#requirements", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Before you begin System requirements \n\t\t\t\t\t Hardware needs vary with the desktop or window manager you select. Lightweight window managers can run on less memory, while full desktop environments and gaming benefit from more resources. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Minimum · lightweight WM Processor 64-bit x86_64 dual-core Memory 2 GB RAM Storage 20 GB available Graphics Compatible graphics hardware Network Internet required \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Recommended · full desktop Processor 64-bit quad-core Memory 4 GB or more; 8 GB for gaming Storage 30 GB or more SSD Graphics Compatible graphics hardware Network Broadband connection \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t An internet connection is required The Zelix Installer downloads current packages from Arch mirrors during setup. Connect using Ethernet or Wi-Fi before starting installation. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Before you begin System requirements \n\t\t\t\t\t Hardware needs vary with the desktop or window manager you select. Lightweight window managers can run on less memory, while full desktop environments and gaming benefit from more resources. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Minimum · lightweight WM Processor 64-bit x86_64 dual-core Memory 2 GB RAM Storage 20 GB available Graphics Compatible graphics hardware Network Internet required \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Recommended · full desktop Processor 64-bit quad-core Memory 4 GB or more; 8 GB for gaming Storage 30 GB or more SSD Graphics Compatible graphics hardware Network Broadband connection \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t An internet connection is required The Zelix Installer downloads current packages from Arch mirrors during setup. Connect using Ethernet or Wi-Fi before starting installation. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Download and verify", "url": "docs-download.html#download", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Get the image Download and verify \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS provides a unified ISO. The desktop environment or window manager is selected during installation, so you do not need a separate image for each desktop. Download the latest image from the  official download page . \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Get the official ISO Use  zelixos.com/download/  and read its release notes. Compare the hash only with an official SHA-256 value for that exact ISO, if one is provided. 02 Verify on Linux For Aurora 1.0.0, run this from the ISO directory. For another release, replace the filename. Compare the result with the SHA-256 value published for that exact download. sha256sum zelixos-2026.10.26-x86_64.iso 03 Verify on Windows For Aurora 1.0.0, run this in PowerShell from the ISO directory. For another release, replace the filename. Compare the result with the published SHA-256 value. Get-FileHash .\\zelixos-2026.10.26-x86_64.iso -Algorithm SHA256 \n\t\t\t\t\t Use the checksum for the exact release Checksum values are release-specific. If the official download does not provide a matching SHA-256 value, do not treat the calculated value alone as verification. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Get the image Download and verify \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS provides a unified ISO. The desktop environment or window manager is selected during installation, so you do not need a separate image for each desktop. Download the latest image from the  official download page . \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Get the official ISO Use  zelixos.com/download/  and read its release notes. Compare the hash only with an official SHA-256 value for that exact ISO, if one is provided. 02 Verify on Linux For Aurora 1.0.0, run this from the ISO directory. For another release, replace the filename. Compare the result with the SHA-256 value published for that exact download. sha256sum zelixos-2026.10.26-x86_64.iso 03 Verify on Windows For Aurora 1.0.0, run this in PowerShell from the ISO directory. For another release, replace the filename. Compare the result with the published SHA-256 value. Get-FileHash .\\zelixos-2026.10.26-x86_64.iso -Algorithm SHA256 \n\t\t\t\t\t Use the checksum for the exact release Checksum values are release-specific. If the official download does not provide a matching SHA-256 value, do not treat the calculated value alone as verification. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Prepare installation media", "url": "docs-usb-prep.html#usb-prep", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Preparation Prepare installation media \n\t\t\t\t\t Use a USB drive with at least 8 GB of capacity. Back up its files before writing the ISO. The current Aurora release recommends UEFI boot with Secure Boot disabled; check your firmware settings if the live USB does not start. \n\t\t\t\t\t Windows Rufus and balenaEtcher are supported choices. In Rufus, select the USB drive and ISO; if prompted for the image writing mode, choose  DD Image mode . In balenaEtcher, choose the ISO file, target USB, and start flashing. \n\t\t\t\t\t Linux and macOS A graphical image writer is recommended. If using the terminal, identify the whole USB device first and verify its name carefully; selecting the wrong device can destroy data on another disk. \n\t\t\t\t\t lsblk \n\t\t\t\t\t Use a USB drive with at least 8 GB capacity and back up its files first. Write the ISO to the whole device, not a partition such as  /dev/sdb1 . Restart the computer, open the one-time boot menu, and choose the USB device. Connect to the internet in the live environment before launching installation. \n\t\t\t\t\t Data loss warning Writing an ISO erases the USB drive. Installation can also format the selected system disk. Back up files and verify every device selection before continuing. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Preparation Prepare installation media \n\t\t\t\t\t Use a USB drive with at least 8 GB of capacity. Back up its files before writing the ISO. The current Aurora release recommends UEFI boot with Secure Boot disabled; check your firmware settings if the live USB does not start. \n\t\t\t\t\t Windows Rufus and balenaEtcher are supported choices. In Rufus, select the USB drive and ISO; if prompted for the image writing mode, choose  DD Image mode . In balenaEtcher, choose the ISO file, target USB, and start flashing. \n\t\t\t\t\t Linux and macOS A graphical image writer is recommended. If using the terminal, identify the whole USB device first and verify its name carefully; selecting the wrong device can destroy data on another disk. \n\t\t\t\t\t lsblk \n\t\t\t\t\t Use a USB drive with at least 8 GB capacity and back up its files first. Write the ISO to the whole device, not a partition such as  /dev/sdb1 . Restart the computer, open the one-time boot menu, and choose the USB device. Connect to the internet in the live environment before launching installation. \n\t\t\t\t\t Data loss warning Writing an ISO erases the USB drive. Installation can also format the selected system disk. Back up files and verify every device selection before continuing. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Zelix Installer", "url": "docs-installer.html#installer", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Guided setup Zelix Installer \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS 1.0.0 includes the Zelix Installer, a graphical setup tool built around the official  archinstall  library. In the live environment, connect to the internet and open  Install ZelixOS  from the desktop. \n\t\t\t\t\t The Zelix Installer welcome screen, with the installation stages listed in the sidebar. \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Welcome and system scan The installer checks basic hardware, boot mode, and network availability. Resolve connection issues before continuing. 02 Select a desktop and greeter Choose from the desktop options presented by your installer, including KDE Plasma, GNOME, Xfce, Hyprland, Sway, i3, or bspwm. Display-manager choices may include SDDM, GDM, LightDM, or Ly. The installer also lets you choose whether an AUR helper will be installed. Select it only if you plan to use AUR packages. 03 Select the disk and bootloader Review the detected NVMe, SSD, or HDD devices and choose the target carefully. Configure the available bootloader option, such as systemd-boot or GRUB. Choose the filesystem and layout shown by your installer; check each formatting action in its final summary. 04 Configure accounts Set the hostname, a strong root password, and your everyday user account. Keep credentials private and store them securely. 05 Install and review progress Confirm the configuration before starting. The installer shows a live log while packages are downloaded and installed; do not power off during this process. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before you confirm Check that the selected target is the intended disk, especially when multiple drives are attached. Review every partition marked for formatting. If another operating system must remain, do not continue until its partitions are preserved. Check boot mode, desktop choice, user account, and the optional AUR helper choice in the final summary. \n\t\t\t\t\t Review the disk summary Disk formatting is destructive. If you need to preserve another operating system or existing files, stop and verify the partition plan before starting. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Installing on an empty dedicated disk Back up any data that might still be on the disk. In the installer, compare the disk model and capacity with the physical drive before selecting it. Review the final summary to see which partitions will be created or formatted. Confirm only when the entire selected disk may be used for ZelixOS. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Keeping another operating system Make a full backup of that system first. Identify its disk and EFI partition before opening the installer. If the current installer does not show a partition layout that clearly preserves them, stop; do not guess at a destructive option. Using a separate disk can simplify the layout, but you still need to check which disk receives the boot entry. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t If installation stops Stay in the live session, keep the network connected, and copy the exact stage and error message. Note which desktop, bootloader, disk, and optional AUR helper choices were made. Avoid restarting or reformatting until you have checked the logs shown by Zelix Installer and identified the failed step. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n                         A practical installation walkthrough \n                         1. Prepare and start the live session Back up the files you need, check the  system requirements , and  verify the downloaded ISO . Write it to a USB drive using the  installation media guide . Boot from the USB using your firmware's boot menu. Connect to the internet in the live desktop and confirm that a website opens before starting Install ZelixOS. \n                         2. Identify the target disk Disconnect unnecessary external drives if practical. In a terminal,  lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS  lists disks and partitions; use the model and size together to identify the target. This command only displays information. The live USB also appears in the list, so do not select a device based on its name alone. lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS \n                         3. Review setup choices Choose the language, desktop, login manager, disk layout, bootloader and account options offered by your installer version. Check that the selected disk and every formatting action match your plan. If preserving an existing system, verify its partitions and EFI partition will be retained; stop if the summary does not make this clear. Store the credentials somewhere secure. \n                         4. Install, then start the installed system Read the final summary before confirming. Keep power and internet connected while the installer runs. Once it reports success, restart and remove the USB when appropriate. Select the installed system in the firmware boot menu if needed, then sign in with the account you created. Continue with  post-installation ; if it does not boot, see  boot and recovery . \n                         When something goes wrong Record the exact message and installation stage, along with the ISO version, target disk, boot mode, desktop and bootloader choices. Check the connection and available space, then consult  troubleshooting . Do not share passwords or private details from logs.", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Guided setup Zelix Installer \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS 1.0.0 includes the Zelix Installer, a graphical setup tool built around the official  archinstall  library. In the live environment, connect to the internet and open  Install ZelixOS  from the desktop. \n\t\t\t\t\t The Zelix Installer welcome screen, with the installation stages listed in the sidebar. \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Welcome and system scan The installer checks basic hardware, boot mode, and network availability. Resolve connection issues before continuing. 02 Select a desktop and greeter Choose from the desktop options presented by your installer, including KDE Plasma, GNOME, Xfce, Hyprland, Sway, i3, or bspwm. Display-manager choices may include SDDM, GDM, LightDM, or Ly. The installer also lets you choose whether an AUR helper will be installed. Select it only if you plan to use AUR packages. 03 Select the disk and bootloader Review the detected NVMe, SSD, or HDD devices and choose the target carefully. Configure the available bootloader option, such as systemd-boot or GRUB. Choose the filesystem and layout shown by your installer; check each formatting action in its final summary. 04 Configure accounts Set the hostname, a strong root password, and your everyday user account. Keep credentials private and store them securely. 05 Install and review progress Confirm the configuration before starting. The installer shows a live log while packages are downloaded and installed; do not power off during this process. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before you confirm Check that the selected target is the intended disk, especially when multiple drives are attached. Review every partition marked for formatting. If another operating system must remain, do not continue until its partitions are preserved. Check boot mode, desktop choice, user account, and the optional AUR helper choice in the final summary. \n\t\t\t\t\t Review the disk summary Disk formatting is destructive. If you need to preserve another operating system or existing files, stop and verify the partition plan before starting. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Boş ve yalnızca ZelixOS’a ayrılmış diske kurulum Diskte hâlâ bulunabilecek verileri yedekleyin. Yükleyicide disk modelini ve kapasitesini fiziksel sürücüyle karşılaştırıp hedefi seçin. Son özette hangi bölümlerin oluşturulacağını veya biçimlendirileceğini inceleyin. Yalnızca seçilen diskin tamamı ZelixOS için kullanılabiliyorsa onaylayın. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Başka bir işletim sistemini koruyarak kurulum Önce o sistemin tam yedeğini alın. Yükleyiciyi açmadan diskini ve EFI bölümünü belirleyin. Mevcut yükleyici onları açıkça koruyan bir bölüm düzeni göstermiyorsa durun; veri silecek bir seçeneği tahmin ederek kullanmayın. Ayrı disk düzeni sadeleştirebilir, ancak önyükleme girdisinin hangi diske yazılacağını yine de kontrol edin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Kurulum durursa Canlı oturumda kalın, ağ bağlantısını açık tutun ve aşama ile hata iletisini aynen kaydedin. Seçilen masaüstünü, önyükleyiciyi, diski ve isteğe bağlı AUR yardımcısını not edin. Zelix Yükleyici’nin gösterdiği günlükleri inceleyip başarısız adımı belirlemeden yeniden başlatmayın veya diski tekrar biçimlendirmeyin. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t \n                         Adım adım kurulum \n                         1. Hazırlık ve canlı oturum Gerekli dosyalarınızı yedekleyin,  sistem gereksinimlerini  kontrol edin ve  indirdiğiniz ISO’yu doğrulayın .  Kurulum medyası rehberiyle  USB hazırlayın. Bilgisayarın önyükleme menüsünden USB’yi başlatın. Canlı masaüstünde internete bağlanın ve ZelixOS kurulumunu açmadan önce bir web sitesinin yüklendiğini doğrulayın. \n                         2. Hedef diski belirleyin Mümkünse gerekli olmayan harici sürücüleri çıkarın. Terminalde  lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS  diskleri ve bölümleri listeler; hedefi belirlemek için model ve kapasiteyi birlikte kontrol edin. Bu komut yalnızca bilgi gösterir. Canlı USB de listede görünür; yalnızca aygıt adına bakarak seçim yapmayın. lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS \n                         3. Kurulum seçimlerini gözden geçirin Yükleyici sürümünüzün sunduğu dil, masaüstü, giriş yöneticisi, disk düzeni, önyükleyici ve hesap seçeneklerini belirleyin. Seçilen diskin ve her biçimlendirme işleminin planınıza uyduğunu kontrol edin. Başka bir sistemi koruyorsanız bölümlerinin ve EFI bölümünün korunacağını doğrulayın; özet açık değilse durun. Giriş bilgilerinizi güvenli bir yerde saklayın. \n                         4. Kurun ve kurulu sistemi başlatın Onaylamadan önce son özeti okuyun. Kurulum sırasında güç ve internet bağlantısını koruyun. Başarı bildirildikten sonra yeniden başlatın ve uygun zamanda USB’yi çıkarın. Gerekirse önyükleme menüsünden kurulu sistemi seçin ve oluşturduğunuz hesapla giriş yapın.  Kurulum sonrası  adımlarla devam edin; sistem açılmazsa  önyükleme ve kurtarma  rehberine bakın. \n                         Bir sorunla karşılaşırsanız Hata mesajını ve kurulum aşamasını aynen kaydedin; ISO sürümünü, hedef diski, önyükleme kipini, masaüstü ve önyükleyici seçimlerini not edin. Bağlantıyı ve boş alanı kontrol edip  sorun giderme  rehberine bakın. Günlüklerdeki parolaları ve özel bilgileri paylaşmayın."}, {"title": "Post-installation", "url": "docs-post-install.html#post-install", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · First boot Post-installation \n\t\t\t\t\t After the first boot, connect to a network and apply available system updates. Zelix Hello opens as an onboarding dashboard and points to common first-run tasks and resources. \n\t\t\t\t\t Zelix Hello brings first-run links and support resources together. \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Check your connection Confirm that wired or wireless networking works. A connection is needed to retrieve repository packages. 02 Synchronize mirrors and update Use Zelix Hello or the updater to review mirrors and apply available system updates. Avoid interrupting package operations. 03 Set up your workspace When you need an application, check Zelix Hello → Software first and install it from the matching category. Check system settings for language, display, audio, power, and network preferences. 04 Keep a recovery path Keep installation media available and make regular backups before major system changes. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · First boot Post-installation \n\t\t\t\t\t After the first boot, connect to a network and apply available system updates. Zelix Hello opens as an onboarding dashboard and points to common first-run tasks and resources. \n\t\t\t\t\t Zelix Hello brings first-run links and support resources together. \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Check your connection Confirm that wired or wireless networking works. A connection is needed to retrieve repository packages. 02 Synchronize mirrors and update Use Zelix Hello or the updater to review mirrors and apply available system updates. Avoid interrupting package operations. 03 Set up your workspace When you need an application, check Zelix Hello → Software first and install it from the matching category. Check system settings for language, display, audio, power, and network preferences. 04 Keep a recovery path Keep installation media available and make regular backups before major system changes. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Boot and recovery", "url": "docs-boot-recovery.html#boot-recovery", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Recovery Boot and recovery \n\t\t\t\t\t If the computer starts the old system after installation, remove the USB drive and open the firmware boot menu. Look for the ZelixOS boot entry on the disk you selected. Check that the firmware boot mode matches the mode used to start the installer. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before changing a bootloader Keep the live USB and a backup of important files. Boot from the USB and check whether your installed partitions are visible with  lsblk -f . Record the output and the installer error before changing partitions or reinstalling a bootloader. A repair procedure depends on your disk layout, encryption, and selected bootloader. \n\t\t\t\t\t lsblk -f \n\t\t\t\t\t Preserve existing partitions Do not format or delete partitions to solve a boot menu problem. If another operating system is installed, identify its EFI partition before making changes. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Installation · Recovery Boot and recovery \n\t\t\t\t\t If the computer starts the old system after installation, remove the USB drive and open the firmware boot menu. Look for the ZelixOS boot entry on the disk you selected. Check that the firmware boot mode matches the mode used to start the installer. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before changing a bootloader Keep the live USB and a backup of important files. Boot from the USB and check whether your installed partitions are visible with  lsblk -f . Record the output and the installer error before changing partitions or reinstalling a bootloader. A repair procedure depends on your disk layout, encryption, and selected bootloader. \n\t\t\t\t\t lsblk -f \n\t\t\t\t\t Preserve existing partitions Do not format or delete partitions to solve a boot menu problem. If another operating system is installed, identify its EFI partition before making changes. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Install applications", "url": "docs-app-install.html#app-install", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Software · Zelix Hello Install applications with Zelix Hello \n\t\t\t\t\t For everyday applications, start with Zelix Hello rather than searching for a separate download on the web. Its Software page groups supported applications and lets you install an individual program with one click. The available catalog can change between ZelixOS releases. \n\t\t\t\t\t Open the Software option from Zelix Hello to browse the application catalog. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Z Zelix Hello Software APPLICATION CATALOG \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Gaming Tümünü Kur · Install all Steam  Kur RetroArch  Kur Lutris  Kur ProtonTricks  Kur MangoHud  Kur Wine  Kur \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Editing Tümünü Kur · Install all Kdenlive  Kur OBS Studio  Kur GIMP  Kur Blender  Kur \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Example entries based on the Zelix Hello Software screen. The exact catalog may vary by release. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Open Zelix Hello Launch Zelix Hello from the application menu or use the welcome shortcut on the desktop. 02 Choose Software Open the Software page to see the application groups available on your installed version. 03 Select one application Choose the individual app’s  Install  button (shown as  Kur  in the Turkish interface). The group-wide button  Install all / Tümünü Kur  installs every app in that category, so use it only if that is what you want. 04 Let installation finish Keep the computer connected to the internet, approve any system authentication prompt, and wait for the install operation to complete. \n\t\t\t\t\t Examples in the Software catalog \n\t\t\t\t\t Gaming Steam, RetroArch, Lutris, ProtonTricks, MangoHud, and Wine. Editing Kdenlive, OBS Studio, GIMP, and Blender. Browsers and communication Firefox, Chromium, Falkon, and Telegram. Office LibreOffice, Okular, and Calligra. \n\t\t\t\t\t Prefer Zelix Hello when an app is listed there When another guide recommends installing a program, first check Zelix Hello → Software. If it is not listed, use the app’s official installation guidance or the current ZelixOS package-manager documentation. Avoid downloading installers from unfamiliar websites. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Software · Zelix Hello Install applications with Zelix Hello \n\t\t\t\t\t For everyday applications, start with Zelix Hello rather than searching for a separate download on the web. Its Software page groups supported applications and lets you install an individual program with one click. The available catalog can change between ZelixOS releases. \n\t\t\t\t\t Open the Software option from Zelix Hello to browse the application catalog. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Z Zelix Hello Software APPLICATION CATALOG \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Gaming Tümünü Kur · Install all Steam  Kur RetroArch  Kur Lutris  Kur ProtonTricks  Kur MangoHud  Kur Wine  Kur \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Editing Tümünü Kur · Install all Kdenlive  Kur OBS Studio  Kur GIMP  Kur Blender  Kur \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Example entries based on the Zelix Hello Software screen. The exact catalog may vary by release. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t 01 Open Zelix Hello Launch Zelix Hello from the application menu or use the welcome shortcut on the desktop. 02 Choose Software Open the Software page to see the application groups available on your installed version. 03 Select one application Choose the individual app’s  Install  button (shown as  Kur  in the Turkish interface). The group-wide button  Install all / Tümünü Kur  installs every app in that category, so use it only if that is what you want. 04 Let installation finish Keep the computer connected to the internet, approve any system authentication prompt, and wait for the install operation to complete. \n\t\t\t\t\t Examples in the Software catalog \n\t\t\t\t\t Gaming Steam, RetroArch, Lutris, ProtonTricks, MangoHud, and Wine. Editing Kdenlive, OBS Studio, GIMP, and Blender. Browsers and communication Firefox, Chromium, Falkon, and Telegram. Office LibreOffice, Okular, and Calligra. \n\t\t\t\t\t Prefer Zelix Hello when an app is listed there When another guide recommends installing a program, first check Zelix Hello → Software. If it is not listed, use the app’s official installation guidance or the current ZelixOS package-manager documentation. Avoid downloading installers from unfamiliar websites. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "ZelixOS visual themes", "url": "docs-themes.html#themes", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS identity Custom login and boot themes \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS carries its own visual identity beyond the desktop. The system includes custom SDDM, GRUB, and Plymouth themes, bringing the ZelixOS logo and dark visual style to login, startup, and boot selection. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t SDDM login screen The graphical sign-in screen shown before the desktop session starts. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t GRUB boot menu A branded bootloader menu for choosing ZelixOS or available startup options. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Plymouth startup screen The ZelixOS logo appears during the system’s graphical startup sequence. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t When each theme appears \n\t\t\t\t\t GRUB  appears during boot when GRUB is the selected bootloader. Plymouth  is the startup splash shown while the system is loading. SDDM  is the login screen when SDDM is selected as the display manager. Other display managers may use their own appearance. \n\t\t\t\t\t Theme availability depends on system configuration The bootloader and display-manager choices selected during installation affect which branded screens are used. If a theme does not appear, first check which bootloader or display manager is active; changing those components may require additional configuration. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS identity Custom login and boot themes \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS carries its own visual identity beyond the desktop. The system includes custom SDDM, GRUB, and Plymouth themes, bringing the ZelixOS logo and dark visual style to login, startup, and boot selection. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t SDDM login screen The graphical sign-in screen shown before the desktop session starts. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t GRUB boot menu A branded bootloader menu for choosing ZelixOS or available startup options. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Plymouth startup screen The ZelixOS logo appears during the system’s graphical startup sequence. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t When each theme appears \n\t\t\t\t\t GRUB  appears during boot when GRUB is the selected bootloader. Plymouth  is the startup splash shown while the system is loading. SDDM  is the login screen when SDDM is selected as the display manager. Other display managers may use their own appearance. \n\t\t\t\t\t Theme availability depends on system configuration The bootloader and display-manager choices selected during installation affect which branded screens are used. If a theme does not appear, first check which bootloader or display manager is active; changing those components may require additional configuration. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Zelix tools", "url": "docs-tools.html#tools", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Zelix tools \n\t\t\t\t\t Project utilities provide a graphical path to common setup and maintenance tasks. Names and availability may vary between releases. \n\t\t\t\t\t Zelix Updater and the Zelix command-line utility. \n\t\t\t\t\t ZH Zelix Hello Welcome hub with links to documentation, release information, support, project resources, language selection, and a keyboard-shortcuts guide. ZU Zelix Updater Graphical utility for checking and applying system package updates. Z Zelix CLI The  zelix  command offers shortcuts for updates, mirror ranking, cleanup, system information, launching Zelix Hello, language selection, and help. Run  zelix help  to see the commands available in your installed version. \n\t\t\t\t \n                         Using the tools \n                         Zelix Hello: first steps and software Use the welcome screen to find documentation, support and release information. To add an application, open  Software , browse the relevant category and review the available choice before installing. The available actions depend on the version installed; see  installing applications  for other package sources. \n                         Zelix Updater: review and update Connect to the internet, open Zelix Updater and check for updates. Aurora 1.0.1 lists available packages and versions and asks for confirmation before applying them. Review the list, confirm when ready, and follow the process output until it finishes. Do not run another package operation at the same time. If an update fails, save the exact error and see  system maintenance . \n                         Zelix CLI: discover commands Open a terminal and run  zelix help  for the commands supported by your installed version. The CLI includes shortcuts for tasks such as updates, mirror ranking and system information. Read the help for an action before running it, especially for cleanup. Aurora also documents a language setting: replace the example with  en  or  tr . zelix help zelix lang tr \n                         If a tool is unavailable Check the application menu and your release notes; features can differ between releases. In a terminal,  command -v zelix  checks whether the CLI is on your path. Record the tool name, release and exact error before asking for help. See  troubleshooting  for collecting useful diagnostics. command -v zelix", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Zelix tools \n\t\t\t\t\t Project utilities provide a graphical path to common setup and maintenance tasks. Names and availability may vary between releases. \n\t\t\t\t\t Zelix Updater and the Zelix command-line utility. \n\t\t\t\t\t ZH Zelix Hello Welcome hub with links to documentation, release information, support, project resources, language selection, and a keyboard-shortcuts guide. ZU Zelix Updater Graphical utility for checking and applying system package updates. Z Zelix CLI The  zelix  command offers shortcuts for updates, mirror ranking, cleanup, system information, launching Zelix Hello, language selection, and help. Run  zelix help  to see the commands available in your installed version. \n\t\t\t\t \n                         Araçları kullanma \n                         Zelix Hello: ilk adımlar ve yazılımlar Karşılama ekranından belgelere, desteğe ve sürüm bilgilerine ulaşın. Uygulama eklemek için  Software  bölümünü açın, ilgili kategoriye bakın ve kurmadan önce seçeneği inceleyin. Kullanılabilir işlemler kurulu sürüme göre değişir; diğer paket kaynakları için  uygulama kurma  rehberine bakın. \n                         Zelix Updater: inceleyin ve güncelleyin İnternete bağlanın, Zelix Updater’ı açın ve güncellemeleri kontrol edin. Aurora 1.0.1, mevcut paketleri ve sürümlerini listeler ve uygulamadan önce onay ister. Listeyi inceleyin, hazır olduğunuzda onaylayın ve işlem bitene kadar çıktıyı takip edin. Aynı anda başka bir paket işlemi çalıştırmayın. Güncelleme başarısız olursa hatayı aynen kaydedip  sistem bakımı  rehberine bakın. \n                         Zelix CLI: komutları keşfedin Terminal açıp kurulu sürümün desteklediği komutlar için  zelix help  çalıştırın. CLI güncelleme, yansı sıralama ve sistem bilgisi gibi işler için kısayollar içerir. Özellikle temizlik işlemlerinden önce ilgili komutun yardımını okuyun. Aurora’da dil ayarı da belgelenmiştir: örnekte  en  veya  tr  kullanın. zelix help zelix lang tr \n                         Bir araç bulunamıyorsa Uygulama menüsünü ve sürüm notlarını kontrol edin; özellikler sürüme göre değişebilir. Terminalde  command -v zelix , CLI komutunun arama yolunda olup olmadığını kontrol eder. Yardım istemeden önce araç adını, sürümü ve hatayı aynen kaydedin. Yararlı tanılama bilgileri için  sorun giderme  rehberine bakın. command -v zelix"}, {"title": "Packages and AUR", "url": "docs-packages.html#packages", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Software Packages and AUR \n\t\t\t\t\t Use Zelix Hello → Software for apps listed in its catalog. For other official repository packages, use pacman. An AUR helper is optional: the Zelix Installer asks whether to install one. Do not assume that Yay or Paru is present on every installation. \n\t\t\t\t\t Official repositories \n\t\t\t\t\t Keep the entire system current when refreshing package databases. Run these commands in a terminal; replace  package-name  with an actual repository package name. \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo pacman -Syu \n\t\t\t\t\t pacman -Ss package-name \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo pacman -S package-name \n\t\t\t\t\t Avoid partial upgrades Refreshing package databases without upgrading the whole system can cause an unsupported partial upgrade. Avoid running pacman -Sy on its own. Use pacman -Syu for a complete update. \n\t\t\t\t\t Optional AUR helper \n\t\t\t\t\t The AUR contains user-maintained build recipes. If you selected an AUR helper in the installer, run  command -v yay  or  command -v paru  to find which helper is installed. Review a package's build files and source before installing it. Run AUR helpers as your regular user, without  sudo . \n\t\t\t\t\t command -v yay; command -v paru \n\t\t\t\t\t If neither command returns a path, you did not install one or it is unavailable in your current environment. Official packages remain available through pacman. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Find and inspect a package Search repository package names and descriptions with  pacman -Ss . Before installing, use  pacman -Si  to see its repository, version, dependencies, and description. To inspect an installed package, use  pacman -Qi . Replace the example package with the name you found. pacman -Ss firefox pacman -Si firefox pacman -Qi firefox \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Install, remove, and list packages pacman -S  installs a repository package.  pacman -R  removes the named package;  pacman -Rs  also removes dependencies that are no longer needed by other packages. Read the transaction summary before confirming removal.  pacman -Qe  lists explicitly installed packages. These commands affect only pacman packages, not Flatpaks. sudo pacman -S firefox sudo pacman -R firefox pacman -Qe \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Use the helper selected in the installer The AUR is community-maintained. Check whether  yay  or  paru  exists before using its commands. Search with the helper you installed, inspect the build recipe and sources, and run it as your regular user. The examples below are alternatives, not commands to run together. If you declined the helper during installation, the official repositories and Zelix Hello still work. yay -Ss package-name paru -Ss package-name When AUR packages break after a system update, check the helper's output and the package's current build instructions; AUR packages may need rebuilding. Never run a helper with  sudo . \n\t\t\t\t\t\t ArchWiki pacman reference  ·  ArchWiki AUR reference \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Software Packages and AUR \n\t\t\t\t\t Use Zelix Hello → Software for apps listed in its catalog. For other official repository packages, use pacman. An AUR helper is optional: the Zelix Installer asks whether to install one. Do not assume that Yay or Paru is present on every installation. \n\t\t\t\t\t Official repositories \n\t\t\t\t\t Keep the entire system current when refreshing package databases. Run these commands in a terminal; replace  package-name  with an actual repository package name. \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo pacman -Syu \n\t\t\t\t\t pacman -Ss package-name \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo pacman -S package-name \n\t\t\t\t\t Avoid partial upgrades Refreshing package databases without upgrading the whole system can cause an unsupported partial upgrade. Avoid running pacman -Sy on its own. Use pacman -Syu for a complete update. \n\t\t\t\t\t Optional AUR helper \n\t\t\t\t\t The AUR contains user-maintained build recipes. If you selected an AUR helper in the installer, run  command -v yay  or  command -v paru  to find which helper is installed. Review a package's build files and source before installing it. Run AUR helpers as your regular user, without  sudo . \n\t\t\t\t\t command -v yay; command -v paru \n\t\t\t\t\t If neither command returns a path, you did not install one or it is unavailable in your current environment. Official packages remain available through pacman. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Paket arama ve inceleme Depo paketlerinin adlarını ve açıklamalarını  pacman -Ss  ile arayın. Yüklemeden önce  pacman -Si  ile depoyu, sürümü, bağımlılıkları ve açıklamayı görün. Kurulu paketi incelemek için  pacman -Qi  kullanın. Örnekteki paket adını bulduğunuz adla değiştirin. pacman -Ss firefox pacman -Si firefox pacman -Qi firefox \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Paket yükleme, kaldırma ve listeleme pacman -S  depo paketini yükler.  pacman -R  adı verilen paketi kaldırır;  pacman -Rs  başka paketlerin kullanmadığı bağımlılıklarını da kaldırır. Kaldırmayı onaylamadan önce işlem özetini okuyun.  pacman -Qe  açıkça yüklenen paketleri listeler. Bu komutlar Flatpak’ları değil, yalnız pacman paketlerini etkiler. sudo pacman -S firefox sudo pacman -R firefox pacman -Qe \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Yükleyicide seçilen yardımcıyı kullanma AUR, topluluk tarafından yönetilir. Komutlarını kullanmadan önce  yay  veya  paru  yüklü mü kontrol edin. Kurduğunuz yardımcıyla arama yapın, derleme tarifini ve kaynakları inceleyin; yardımcıyı normal kullanıcı olarak çalıştırın. Aşağıdaki örnekler alternatiftir, birlikte çalıştırılmaz. Kurulumda yardımcıyı seçmediyseniz resmî depolar ve Zelix Hello yine çalışır. yay -Ss package-name paru -Ss package-name AUR paketleri sistem güncellemesi sonrası bozulursa yardımcının çıktısını ve paketin güncel derleme yönergelerini inceleyin; yeniden derleme gerekebilir. Yardımcıyı  sudo  ile çalıştırmayın. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t ArchWiki pacman başvurusu  ·  ArchWiki AUR başvurusu \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "System maintenance", "url": "docs-maintenance.html#maintenance", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Rolling release System maintenance \n\t\t\t\t\t Back up personal files before major changes and keep your installation USB available. Read current release notes before a large update, then use Zelix Updater or  sudo pacman -Syu . Let package operations finish and restart when a kernel or driver update requires it. \n\t\t\t\t\t Check free space and configuration changes \n\t\t\t\t\t Low disk space can interrupt downloads and updates. Review free space with  df -h . Package updates may place new configuration defaults in  .pacnew  files; compare these with your edited files and merge needed changes instead of blindly replacing either version. \n\t\t\t\t\t df -h \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo find /etc -name '*.pacnew' -print \n\t\t\t\t\t When an update fails \n\t\t\t\t\t Record the exact error. Check network access, free space, and whether another package process is running. Resolve the cause before retrying a full update. Avoid deleting pacman lock files while a package operation is active. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Before a large update Read the ZelixOS release notes and any relevant Arch news, back up important data, and ensure the system has enough free space and a stable connection. Run one complete update with Zelix Updater or  sudo pacman -Syu . Do not run a second package manager while the first is working. Restart after kernel or driver updates when the tool asks for it. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Back up what matters Keep a copy of personal files and important settings on another drive or trusted storage. A snapshot on the same disk is helpful for some configuration mistakes but will not survive that disk failing. Check that you can actually open a restored file before relying on a backup. Keep the live USB available for boot recovery. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Review .pacnew files and the package cache When an updated package ships a new default configuration, pacman may create a  .pacnew  file. Compare it with your current file and merge the needed settings. Do not overwrite a working configuration blindly. The package cache can help with recovery; inspect its size before cleaning it. Use the Zelix CLI cleanup feature only after reading what your installed version does. sudo find /etc -name '*.pacnew' -print du -sh /var/cache/pacman/pkg \n\t\t\t\t\t\t ArchWiki system maintenance \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Rolling release System maintenance \n\t\t\t\t\t Back up personal files before major changes and keep your installation USB available. Read current release notes before a large update, then use Zelix Updater or  sudo pacman -Syu . Let package operations finish and restart when a kernel or driver update requires it. \n\t\t\t\t\t Check free space and configuration changes \n\t\t\t\t\t Low disk space can interrupt downloads and updates. Review free space with  df -h . Package updates may place new configuration defaults in  .pacnew  files; compare these with your edited files and merge needed changes instead of blindly replacing either version. \n\t\t\t\t\t df -h \n\t\t\t\t\t sudo find /etc -name '*.pacnew' -print \n\t\t\t\t\t When an update fails \n\t\t\t\t\t Record the exact error. Check network access, free space, and whether another package process is running. Resolve the cause before retrying a full update. Avoid deleting pacman lock files while a package operation is active. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Büyük güncelleme öncesinde ZelixOS sürüm notlarını ve ilgili Arch duyurularını okuyun, önemli verileri yedekleyin; yeterli boş alan ve kararlı bağlantı sağlayın. Zelix Updater veya  sudo pacman -Syu  ile tek bir tam güncelleme yapın. İlki çalışırken ikinci paket yöneticisini başlatmayın. Araç gerektiğini belirttiğinde çekirdek veya sürücü güncellemesinden sonra yeniden başlatın. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Önemli verileri yedekleme Kişisel dosyaların ve önemli ayarların bir kopyasını başka bir sürücüde veya güvenilir depolamada tutun. Aynı diskteki anlık görüntü bazı yapılandırma hatalarını geri alabilir, ancak disk bozulursa onu koruyamaz. Yedeğe güvenmeden önce geri yüklenen bir dosyayı gerçekten açabildiğinizi deneyin. Önyükleme kurtarması için canlı USB’yi saklayın. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t .pacnew dosyaları ve paket önbelleği Güncellenen paket yeni varsayılan yapılandırma sunduğunda pacman bir  .pacnew  dosyası oluşturabilir. Mevcut dosyanızla karşılaştırıp gerekli ayarları birleştirin. Çalışan yapılandırmanın üzerine düşünmeden yazmayın. Paket önbelleği kurtarmada işe yarayabilir; temizlemeden önce boyutunu inceleyin. Zelix CLI temizleme özelliğini yalnızca kurulu sürümün ne yaptığını okuduktan sonra kullanın. sudo find /etc -name '*.pacnew' -print du -sh /var/cache/pacman/pkg \n\t\t\t\t\t\t ArchWiki sistem bakımı \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Hardware and drivers", "url": "docs-hardware.html#hardware", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Hardware Hardware and drivers \n\t\t\t\t\t Start with the desktop's settings for displays, audio, networking, and Bluetooth. Keep a full system update in place before diagnosing a device. Hardware and driver choices vary by model, kernel, and desktop session. \n\t\t\t\t\t Identify graphics and network devices Use  lspci -k  to see PCI devices and their active kernel drivers. For USB Wi-Fi devices, use  lsusb . Include the relevant device line and kernel version when requesting support. \n\t\t\t\t\t lspci -k uname -r \n\t\t\t\t\t Sound and Bluetooth Check the selected output and input in your desktop's audio settings before changing services. If Bluetooth devices are missing, verify that the adapter is enabled and not blocked by airplane mode. Record the exact device model and error before installing extra drivers. \n\t\t\t\t\t NVIDIA and hybrid graphics Driver packages depend on the GPU generation and installed kernel. Identify the hardware and current driver first; do not copy a generic driver command onto every machine. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Hardware Hardware and drivers \n\t\t\t\t\t Start with the desktop's settings for displays, audio, networking, and Bluetooth. Keep a full system update in place before diagnosing a device. Hardware and driver choices vary by model, kernel, and desktop session. \n\t\t\t\t\t Identify graphics and network devices Use  lspci -k  to see PCI devices and their active kernel drivers. For USB Wi-Fi devices, use  lsusb . Include the relevant device line and kernel version when requesting support. \n\t\t\t\t\t lspci -k uname -r \n\t\t\t\t\t Sound and Bluetooth Check the selected output and input in your desktop's audio settings before changing services. If Bluetooth devices are missing, verify that the adapter is enabled and not blocked by airplane mode. Record the exact device model and error before installing extra drivers. \n\t\t\t\t\t NVIDIA and hybrid graphics Driver packages depend on the GPU generation and installed kernel. Identify the hardware and current driver first; do not copy a generic driver command onto every machine. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Gaming", "url": "docs-gaming.html#gaming", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Gaming \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS is based on Arch Linux, so gaming applications and compatibility tools can be installed from supported repositories. Availability and compatibility depend on your hardware, game, and current package versions. \n\t\t\t\t\t Install gaming tools Open  Zelix Hello → Software → Gaming  to install Steam, RetroArch, Lutris, ProtonTricks, MangoHud, or Wine from the available catalog. Select an individual Install button; you do not need to use “Install all” to choose a single app. If an app is not shown, check the current ZelixOS installation guidance before using another source. \n\t\t\t\t\t Steam and Proton After installing Steam, sign in and open its settings. Enable Steam Play and select Proton for Windows titles; compatibility differs by game and Proton version. Steam may need to download additional runtime files the first time you launch a game. \n\t\t\t\t\t Drivers and performance Use the driver appropriate for your Intel, AMD, or NVIDIA hardware and keep the system updated. Avoid mixing driver packages from unrelated sources. Allow extra memory and SSD space for game installations; the system requirements section recommends 8 GB RAM for gaming and heavy multitasking. \n\t\t\t\t\t Confirm that the GPU is detected and the expected driver is active. Check free storage before downloading large game libraries. If a game fails to start, test its supported Proton version and check the game’s compatibility reports. When asking for help, include the game title, hardware, driver, Proton version, and relevant error output. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before changing repositories Follow current Arch and ZelixOS guidance when enabling additional repositories or installing third-party packages. \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Using ZelixOS Gaming \n\t\t\t\t\t ZelixOS is based on Arch Linux, so gaming applications and compatibility tools can be installed from supported repositories. Availability and compatibility depend on your hardware, game, and current package versions. \n\t\t\t\t\t Install gaming tools Open  Zelix Hello → Software → Gaming  to install Steam, RetroArch, Lutris, ProtonTricks, MangoHud, or Wine from the available catalog. Select an individual Install button; you do not need to use “Install all” to choose a single app. If an app is not shown, check the current ZelixOS installation guidance before using another source. \n\t\t\t\t\t Steam and Proton After installing Steam, sign in and open its settings. Enable Steam Play and select Proton for Windows titles; compatibility differs by game and Proton version. Steam may need to download additional runtime files the first time you launch a game. \n\t\t\t\t\t Drivers and performance Use the driver appropriate for your Intel, AMD, or NVIDIA hardware and keep the system updated. Avoid mixing driver packages from unrelated sources. Allow extra memory and SSD space for game installations; the system requirements section recommends 8 GB RAM for gaming and heavy multitasking. \n\t\t\t\t\t Confirm that the GPU is detected and the expected driver is active. Check free storage before downloading large game libraries. If a game fails to start, test its supported Proton version and check the game’s compatibility reports. When asking for help, include the game title, hardware, driver, Proton version, and relevant error output. \n\t\t\t\t\t Before changing repositories Follow current Arch and ZelixOS guidance when enabling additional repositories or installing third-party packages. \n\t\t\t\t"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "url": "docs-troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting", "en": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Support Troubleshooting \n\t\t\t\t\t Start with these basic checks before changing system configuration. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Use the checks below from the affected installed system unless a step says live USB. Start with read-only commands and record what you find. A command missing on your installation is useful information; do not install random packages just to make a diagnostic command run. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 1. Collect the basics Note the ZelixOS release, desktop, session type, kernel, hardware, and when the problem started. The commands below show the running kernel, PCI devices, disk layout, and recent errors from this boot. System logs may need administrator rights. Check output for private names, paths, and addresses before sharing. uname -r lspci -k lsblk -f sudo journalctl -b -p err --no-pager -n 80 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 2. Desktop will not open or login loops At the greeter, select the desktop that was installed. If the screen returns to the greeter, switch to a text console with Ctrl+Alt+F3 and sign in. Check free space and failed user services. A full root partition can prevent sessions from starting. Record recent user journal messages; do not delete desktop configuration files before backing them up. df -h systemctl --user --failed journalctl --user -b --no-pager -n 80 If the text console also fails, use the live USB to inspect disks and collect the visible error. A blank graphical screen after changing a Hyprland, Sway, i3, or bspwm config should prompt a check of that config and its most recent edit. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 3. Network connects but downloads fail First check whether websites load and whether the problem affects every application or only pacman. If NetworkManager is present,  nmcli device status  shows device state.  ip route  shows the selected route. A missing route points to a connection problem; a pacman-only failure can indicate an outdated mirror or package database. Use Zelix Hello's mirror action or a full system update after confirming connectivity. nmcli device status ip route sudo pacman -Syu Never use  pacman -Sy  alone as a workaround. If a mirror returns 404, note the package name and mirror URL before changing settings. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 4. Updates stop or pacman says the database is locked Check whether Zelix Updater, pacman, or an AUR helper is still running. A lock can protect an active transaction. Wait for the operation to finish; never remove the lock while it is active. If an operation was interrupted, record the exact error and ask for help with the stale lock after verifying all package processes have stopped. Check free space and retry a full update only after the cause is clear. ps -ef | grep -E '[p]acman|[y]ay|[p]aru' df -h \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 5. No audio, microphone, or Bluetooth Check the selected input and output in your desktop settings, mute state, and the app's own device selection. For PipeWire systems,  wpctl status  lists sinks and sources. If that command is unavailable, record it and check whether PipeWire and WirePlumber are running for your user. Bluetooth issues should also be checked against airplane mode and adapter state. wpctl status systemctl --user status pipewire wireplumber Do not restart or replace audio services until you know which component is failing. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 6. A monitor is missing or the screen is black Test the cable and input selection first. KDE, GNOME, and Xfce provide display settings. In Hyprland use  hyprctl monitors ; in Sway use  swaymsg -t get_outputs ; in i3 use  i3-msg -t get_outputs . Note whether the display is detected, which session type you use, and the GPU driver reported by  lspci -k . Do not install a generic NVIDIA package before identifying the card and kernel. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 7. What to include in a support report Write a short title describing the symptom. Include the ISO/release, desktop or WM, Wayland or X11, hardware model, exact error text, steps to reproduce, what you already tried, and relevant command output. State whether the problem started after an update or a configuration change. Redact account names, Wi-Fi credentials, tokens, and other private data. ZelixOS project and issue tracker \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The live USB will not start Verify the ISO against the checksum for its release, then write it to the entire USB device again. Try the firmware's one-time boot menu. Aurora 1.0.0 recommends UEFI with Secure Boot disabled. Record any on-screen error before changing firmware settings. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The installer cannot connect to the internet Connect from the live desktop's network controls, then open a website to confirm access. Try Ethernet if Wi-Fi is unavailable. Record the network adapter model and the exact installer error if it still fails. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The installer cannot see the target disk Check that the disk appears in the firmware and in the live session with  lsblk -f . Record the disk model and current storage-controller setting. Do not change controller mode or erase partitions without a backup and a recovery plan for any existing operating system. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The computer boots to the old operating system Remove the USB drive and select the installed ZelixOS entry from the firmware boot menu. If it is absent, follow the  boot and recovery  checks and record the boot mode and partition layout. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t An update fails Record the complete error, check the network and free space with  df -h , and confirm that another package operation is not running. Fix the cause and retry a full update. Do not delete the pacman lock file while an update is active. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t No sound or microphone Check the selected input and output in the desktop's audio settings and test another application. If sound still fails, record the device name and the output of  systemctl --user status pipewire wireplumber  for a support report. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t I need more help Report the ZelixOS release, desktop, hardware model, exact error, and steps to reproduce it in the  ZelixOS GitHub . Remove passwords and other private information from logs before sharing them. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t", "tr": "\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Support Troubleshooting \n\t\t\t\t\t Start with these basic checks before changing system configuration. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t Aksi belirtilmedikçe aşağıdaki kontrolleri sorun yaşanan kurulu sistemde yapın; canlı USB adımlarını ayrıca belirttik. Önce yalnızca bilgi okuyan komutları kullanıp bulguları kaydedin. Bir komutun kurulu sistemde bulunmaması da yararlı bilgidir; sırf tanılama komutu çalışsın diye rastgele paket yüklemeyin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 1. Temel bilgileri toplayın ZelixOS sürümünü, masaüstünü, oturum türünü, çekirdeği, donanımı ve sorunun ne zaman başladığını not edin. Aşağıdaki komutlar çalışan çekirdeği, PCI aygıtlarını, disk düzenini ve bu açılıştaki son hataları gösterir. Sistem günlükleri yönetici yetkisi isteyebilir. Paylaşmadan önce çıktıda özel ad, yol ve adres olup olmadığını kontrol edin. uname -r lspci -k lsblk -f sudo journalctl -b -p err --no-pager -n 80 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 2. Masaüstü açılmıyor veya giriş döngüsü yaşanıyor Giriş ekranında kurduğunuz masaüstünü seçin. Ekran tekrar giriş ekranına dönüyorsa Ctrl+Alt+F3 ile metin konsoluna geçip oturum açın. Boş alanı ve başarısız kullanıcı servislerini kontrol edin. Dolu kök bölüm oturumun açılmasını engelleyebilir. Son kullanıcı günlüklerini kaydedin; masaüstü yapılandırma dosyalarını yedeklemeden silmeyin. df -h systemctl --user --failed journalctl --user -b --no-pager -n 80 Metin konsolu da açılmıyorsa canlı USB ile diskleri inceleyip ekrandaki hatayı kaydedin. Hyprland, Sway, i3 veya bspwm yapılandırması değiştikten sonra siyah ekran oluştuysa dosyanın son düzenlemesini kontrol edin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 3. Ağ bağlı ama indirmeler başarısız Önce sitelerin açılıp açılmadığına, sorunun tüm uygulamalarda mı yalnız pacman’da mı görüldüğüne bakın. NetworkManager varsa  nmcli device status  aygıt durumunu gösterir.  ip route  seçilen rotayı gösterir. Rota yoksa bağlantı sorunu olabilir; yalnız pacman hata veriyorsa yansı veya paket veritabanı güncelliğini kontrol edin. Bağlantıyı doğruladıktan sonra Zelix Hello’nun yansı aracını ya da tam sistem güncellemesini kullanın. nmcli device status ip route sudo pacman -Syu Geçici çözüm olarak  pacman -Sy  komutunu tek başına çalıştırmayın. Bir yansı 404 döndürüyorsa ayarları değiştirmeden önce paket adını ve yansı adresini kaydedin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 4. Güncelleme duruyor veya pacman veritabanı kilitli diyor Zelix Updater, pacman veya AUR yardımcısının hâlâ çalışıp çalışmadığını kontrol edin. Kilit, etkin işlemi koruyor olabilir. İşlem bitene kadar bekleyin; etkin işlem sırasında kilidi silmeyin. İşlem yarıda kesildiyse tam hatayı kaydedin ve bütün paket süreçlerinin durduğunu doğruladıktan sonra eski kilit için yardım isteyin. Nedeni anlamadan tam güncellemeyi tekrarlamayın; boş alanı da kontrol edin. ps -ef | grep -E '[p]acman|[y]ay|[p]aru' df -h \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 5. Ses, mikrofon veya Bluetooth çalışmıyor Masaüstü ayarlarında seçilen giriş ve çıkışı, sessiz modunu ve uygulamanın kendi aygıt seçimini kontrol edin. PipeWire sistemlerinde  wpctl status  ses çıkış ve girişlerini listeler. Komut yoksa bunu not edin ve kullanıcı için PipeWire ile WirePlumber’ın çalışıp çalışmadığını inceleyin. Bluetooth için uçak modunu ve bağdaştırıcının etkinliğini de kontrol edin. wpctl status systemctl --user status pipewire wireplumber Hangi bileşenin bozuk olduğunu anlamadan ses servislerini yeniden başlatmayın veya değiştirmeyin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 6. Ekran görünmüyor veya siyah kalıyor Önce kabloyu ve monitörün giriş seçimini deneyin. KDE, GNOME ve Xfce ekran ayarları sunar. Hyprland’da  hyprctl monitors , Sway’de  swaymsg -t get_outputs , i3’te  i3-msg -t get_outputs  kullanın. Ekranın algılanıp algılanmadığını, oturum türünü ve  lspci -k  çıktısındaki GPU sürücüsünü not edin. Kartı ve çekirdeği belirlemeden genel bir NVIDIA paketi yüklemeyin. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 7. Destek bildirimine neler eklemeli? Belirtiyi anlatan kısa bir başlık yazın. ISO/sürüm, masaüstü veya pencere yöneticisi, Wayland ya da X11, donanım modeli, tam hata metni, tekrarlama adımları, denedikleriniz ve ilgili komut çıktılarını ekleyin. Sorunun güncelleme veya yapılandırma değişikliği sonrasında başlayıp başlamadığını belirtin. Hesap adlarını, Wi-Fi parolalarını, anahtarları ve diğer özel bilgileri gizleyin. ZelixOS projesi ve hata takibi \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The live USB will not start Verify the ISO against the checksum for its release, then write it to the entire USB device again. Try the firmware's one-time boot menu. Aurora 1.0.0 recommends UEFI with Secure Boot disabled. Record any on-screen error before changing firmware settings. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The installer cannot connect to the internet Connect from the live desktop's network controls, then open a website to confirm access. Try Ethernet if Wi-Fi is unavailable. Record the network adapter model and the exact installer error if it still fails. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The installer cannot see the target disk Check that the disk appears in the firmware and in the live session with  lsblk -f . Record the disk model and current storage-controller setting. Do not change controller mode or erase partitions without a backup and a recovery plan for any existing operating system. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t The computer boots to the old operating system Remove the USB drive and select the installed ZelixOS entry from the firmware boot menu. If it is absent, follow the  boot and recovery  checks and record the boot mode and partition layout. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t An update fails Record the complete error, check the network and free space with  df -h , and confirm that another package operation is not running. Fix the cause and retry a full update. Do not delete the pacman lock file while an update is active. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t No sound or microphone Check the selected input and output in the desktop's audio settings and test another application. If sound still fails, record the device name and the output of  systemctl --user status pipewire wireplumber  for a support report. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t I need more help Report the ZelixOS release, desktop, hardware model, exact error, and steps to reproduce it in the  ZelixOS GitHub . Remove passwords and other private information from logs before sharing them. \n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t"}];
